{"login": "itislu", "location": "Vienna, Austria", "commits": [{"sha": "5ddabc55c993edde404272d573e8539560acde89", "message": "wip", "created_at": "2026-02-03T21:21:02Z", "repo": "42-Libft", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "4370aee2f71865a708d6c43ffc8344bd492fd129", "message": "fix(`ft_memmove`): Cast pointer to `uintptr_t` only from `void *`\n\nThe C standard explicitly mentions pointer to void:\n\"The following type designates an unsigned integer type with the\nproperty that any valid pointer to void can be converted to this type,\nthen converted back to pointer to void, and the result will compare\nequal to the original pointer: uintptr_t\"", "created_at": "2026-02-03T21:20:15Z", "repo": "42-Libft", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "23d3d9d4d2f960e4cf75ea8c86d47c44b9adab64", "message": "fix(`ft_memmove`): Use `uintptr_t` for comparing pointers to avoid UB\n\nComparing pointers that point to different objects with relational\noperators is UB in C.\nNote however that `uintptr_t` is an optional type, so it may still not\nbe portable to all platforms.", "created_at": "2026-01-11T18:30:10Z", "repo": "42-Libft", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "4a503696f22e0aafd779cae656e96958c439ada5", "message": "refactor(`ft_printf`): Use `uintptr_t` for `%p`\n\n`uintptr_t` is capable of holding any pointer type, but it is an optional type. A guaranteed alternative would be `uintmax_t`. But for now, I like that `uintptr_t` communicates that it stores a pointer address. If it is not available, pointers on that system might have some metadata and could not be easily printed anyway.", "created_at": "2025-07-10T14:01:48Z", "repo": "42-Libft", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "648d0a1d0ebd0b485127116e5ebd8145f49d50f4", "message": "fix: Fix memory leaks if `ft_lst*` function args are `NULL`", "created_at": "2025-05-28T19:37:27Z", "repo": "42-Libft", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "b0a0dfc8e5a281a1a237b084c7a7603ba6f303e8", "message": "style: Rename `*_eff` functions to `*_tail`", "created_at": "2025-05-28T19:31:38Z", "repo": "42-Libft", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "b77afa7c8cc485fc51d51605fad55f06a0aac5ed", "message": "improve: Add compiler attributes to all stdlib functions\n\nUse the same as the original ones use.", "created_at": "2025-03-08T05:23:50Z", "repo": "42-Libft", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "8f57f6f9eec1369c861320c33db0cf1cc209bf6e", "message": "improve(`ft_printf`): Add compiler attributes\n\nThey will throw a compile-time warning when the format string is used incorrectly, same as the original `printf()`.", "created_at": "2025-03-08T05:23:50Z", "repo": "42-Libft", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "fa9e8c3cf40910122f6c4747e792e09a5fd847be", "message": "refactor(`ft_printf`): Use `ft_nbrlen_base()` and `ft_labs()`", "created_at": "2025-03-08T05:23:35Z", "repo": "42-Libft", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "574c68907b00464446c230a55a7f99f3894351c5", "message": "refactor(numbers)!: Adjust `ft_abs` type functions to original ones\n\n`ft_abs()` is now `ft_labs_u()`.\n\nI wasn't aware that `abs()` existed in libc. Having a different prototype for it would be weird.", "created_at": "2025-03-05T22:24:13Z", "repo": "42-Libft", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "f6fecdcc54bcc0b928d444f5da50933243230064", "message": "feat(strings): Add `ft_strcount_str`", "created_at": "2025-03-04T04:31:48Z", "repo": "42-Libft", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "942073e99b33efac004274e6650c94817306820b", "message": "feat(numbers): Add `ft_saturating_sub_u`", "created_at": "2025-03-04T04:31:43Z", "repo": "42-Libft", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "c5ed3fe495d21a3314823cdf1f2d39ecd79ea58b", "message": "docs: Name `NULL` and `NUL` (`'\\0`) consistently", "created_at": "2025-03-04T03:30:39Z", "repo": "42-Libft", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "7d3f68a446bac0227562b68a3aec41bc7c0a1177", "message": "fix(`ft_isspace`): Fix NUL-terminator being counted as whitespace", "created_at": "2025-03-04T03:05:40Z", "repo": "42-Libft", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "816ad4d0864e8aedd153cac3eb6398540a63a980", "message": "fix(`get_next_line`): Don't allow `BUFFER_SIZE` bigger than `SSIZE_MAX`\n\n`man 2 read`: \"According to POSIX.1, if count is greater than SSIZE_MAX, the result is implementation-defined\"\n\nAlso remove `bits/posix1_lim.h` include because it says \"Never include this file directly; use <limits.h> instead.\"", "created_at": "2025-03-02T23:58:49Z", "repo": "42-Libft", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "cfdc9bcd23097430206766c74bbd7abb0ab15a36", "message": "docs: Remove empty line at end of documentations", "created_at": "2025-02-13T02:55:28Z", "repo": "42-Libft", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "2c9ab6692f7c7f5a8e44e8fc16ce0b60c2efa521", "message": "style(`ft_strtrim`): Use `bool`", "created_at": "2025-02-13T02:55:28Z", "repo": "42-Libft", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "7fd4a7a403c2787e00a467e6d5fa14470236826e", "message": "style: Make all comparisons explicit", "created_at": "2025-02-13T02:55:28Z", "repo": "42-Libft", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "1063e96a88ab8029b703ac67b74e9bd1f2700c8b", "message": "refactor(`ft_snprintf`): Call `ft_vsnprintf()` to reuse code", "created_at": "2025-02-13T02:16:59Z", "repo": "42-Libft", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "c2dbbea0e396cb2c7e48396d9ab142d8758e9e96", "message": "fix(`ft_vsnprintf`): Call `va_end()` on copy of `ap`, not the actual argument", "created_at": "2025-02-13T02:16:59Z", "repo": "42-Libft", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "b5356ff77bee64a90a8dc706e426a1603babebc4", "message": "fix(`ft_snprintf`): Correct return value when `size` argument is 0\n\nDeletes unnecessary `ft_sputnchar()` and `ft_sputnstr()` functions and moves `ft_snputnbr_base()` to `strings` directory as `ft_strlcpy_nbr_base()`.", "created_at": "2025-02-13T02:16:59Z", "repo": "42-Libft", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "d849ce79fdd9355f6fb132522b0c7982e889dc4c", "message": "docs(`ft_strlcpy`): Fix wrong claim in description", "created_at": "2025-02-13T02:16:59Z", "repo": "42-Libft", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "b225033cd135b60d4e37a178b8fd2857d8fd5393", "message": "fix(`ft_strlcpy`): Fix return value when dst and src overlap", "created_at": "2025-02-13T02:16:59Z", "repo": "42-Libft", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "5e5e9fcfa39d87e08ef171854ea931132acb2e71", "message": "perf(`ft_strlcpy`): Use `ft_memcpy()`", "created_at": "2025-02-13T02:16:59Z", "repo": "42-Libft", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "7640259c91c80bfb00a070bde76b43245284617c", "message": "fix(`ft_abs`): Fix undefined behavior of signed overflow\n\nUse it in `ft_putnbr_base_fd()` and `ft_snputnbr_base()`.", "created_at": "2025-02-13T02:16:59Z", "repo": "42-Libft", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "a7f77d71f0899cc869a9fa1bc6f88caad8679511", "message": "style(`ft_snprintf`): Change parameter name of internal function", "created_at": "2025-02-13T02:16:59Z", "repo": "42-Libft", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "2c518ba2c3c0c52eec2efdc95cb9087c94c229b3", "message": "fix(`ft_snprintf`): Return the number of characters which the format string would expand to\n\nThey now behave the same as the original `snprintf` and `vsnprintf`.", "created_at": "2025-02-13T02:16:59Z", "repo": "42-Libft", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "ba649cd080e7b3a39dcb1ccfe2b7662352b45e20", "message": "feat(numbers): Add `ft_nbrlen_base` and `ft_nbrlen_base_u`\n\nUse it in `ft_snputnbr_base()`.", "created_at": "2025-02-13T02:16:59Z", "repo": "42-Libft", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "9d2b63472853e76c8016893be98c8f487b131832", "message": "feat(numbers): Add `ft_abs`", "created_at": "2025-02-13T02:16:59Z", "repo": "42-Libft", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "b46dcb5e59dfd638f37422bbfe4e05986fc2b79e", "message": "feat(numbers): Add unsigned versions of of `ft_max`/`ft_min`\n\nAlso:\n- Change types to `long`.\n- Mention to use the `MAX`/`MIN` macros directly if performance is critical and type safety is not needed.\n\nAdds:\n- `ft_max_u`\n- `ft_min_u`\n\nChanges:\n- `ft_max`\n- `ft_min`", "created_at": "2025-02-13T02:16:59Z", "repo": "42-Libft", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "260ef538cb36f8ef4273ee20f967eee156797676", "message": "docs: Change wording from segmentation fault to undefined behavior", "created_at": "2025-02-13T02:16:59Z", "repo": "42-Libft", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "0c04a211412e8aee3fd8a851c2c9393dc699a1e1", "message": "style(`ft_lstsort_bubble`): Make function name more clear", "created_at": "2025-02-13T02:16:59Z", "repo": "42-Libft", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "153b04d01b5b4c9dc668ce145c62c6970178cbaa", "message": "docs(`ft_itoa`): Move to numbers and add documentation that caller is responsible for freeing", "created_at": "2025-02-13T02:16:59Z", "repo": "42-Libft", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "1b1aec3b56c34bd55e78064d6efbf54cc77f586f", "message": "feat(`ft_calloc`): Set `errno` same as original if overflow would occur", "created_at": "2025-02-13T02:16:59Z", "repo": "42-Libft", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "b25283bf7854596cf28d34963dfdd46989adcccd", "message": "feat: Add `ft_inrange_mul_u()` to libft\n\nUse it in `ft_calloc()`.", "created_at": "2025-02-13T02:16:59Z", "repo": "42-Libft", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "d4b9fa9e236ab7d73d6aef70322c77c008d78e68", "message": "style(`get_next_line`): Use `bool`", "created_at": "2025-02-13T02:16:57Z", "repo": "42-Libft", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "cd2c2f6ab2020975fb44ab54bc81ea49613ccc7b", "message": "chore(`ft_itoa`): Use `unsigned` for char counter", "created_at": "2025-02-04T21:33:51Z", "repo": "42-Libft", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "ccb5bf7dae9af9ff5d31803757e1c1123fa4acea", "message": "style: Reduce indentation", "created_at": "2025-02-04T21:33:51Z", "repo": "42-Libft", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "759cb4892a76231cfa7d8d6d216327040557f981", "message": "chore(`ft_strmatches_any`): Pass `va_list` safely by reference", "created_at": "2025-02-04T21:33:51Z", "repo": "42-Libft", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "77b9fe9ac995c2e6a663eff7d78ead86f11c8de9", "message": "chore: Fix typo of `occurrence`", "created_at": "2025-02-04T21:33:51Z", "repo": "42-Libft", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "0609fdd4b1c97fa74b4a276a3d3e043a82036901", "message": "refactor: Refactor s